%%{init: {"sequence": {"wrap": true, "width": 210, "noteMargin": 8}}}%%
%% Checkout submit: one CAS plus an outbox row. Never touches Redis or the PSP.
%% Source of docs/diagrams/checkout-submit.svg. The reserve step is in reserve-checkout.mmd.
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor B as Browser
  participant A as api
  participant P as Postgres

  Note over B,A: Checkout page. Idempotency-Key C created once per order, kept in sessionStorage per orderId, so a reload replays
  B->>A: POST /api/v1/orders/:orderId/checkout, Idempotency-Key C, shipping and paymentMethod
  A->>P: BEGIN, CAS RESERVED → PENDING_PAYMENT WHERE owner and not expired, expires_at = now + payment window
  alt CAS won
    A->>P: INSERT outbox order.placed, pg_notify outbox, COMMIT
    A-->>B: 202 PENDING_PAYMENT
  else CAS lost
    A->>P: ROLLBACK, SELECT order
    A-->>B: 200 replay if same key and hash · 422 if hash differs · 409 ALREADY_SUBMITTED if another key · 410 if expired
  end
  Note over B: 409 ALREADY_SUBMITTED → go to /orders/:orderId
  Note over A,P: Checkout never calls Redis or the PSP. The HTTP request ends at the PG commit
